From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] web: an exit from the viewer waits for its own eval

tclExitHandler runs on an io thread, inside TclEvaluator::eval's
Tcl_Eval, and wakes waitForStop() on the main thread. stop() then
restored the original `exit` on the interpreter at once, while the io
thread was still unwinding its evaluation: two threads in one Tcl
interpreter, "TclStackFree: incorrect freePtr" and signal 11. Seen on
bazel-orfs's odb-debug daemon, whose idle exit sends `exit` through
the viewer, as a browser's Tcl box does.

stop() takes the evaluator's mutex, which eval() holds for the whole
evaluation, before it touches the interpreter. Not upstreamed; retires
at the //:bump onto an OpenROAD that serializes the restore.

---
diff --git a/src/web/src/web_serve.cpp b/src/web/src/web_serve.cpp
index 907c1533..1b2b94c6 100644
--- a/src/web/src/web_serve.cpp
+++ b/src/web/src/web_serve.cpp
@@ -651,12 +651,19 @@ void WebServer::stop()
 {
   // Restore the original Tcl `exit` command before tearing down — pairs
   // with the rename in serve().  Skip if not installed (stop() is safe
-  // to call multiple times).
-  if (Tcl_FindCommand(interp_, kRenamedExitCmd, nullptr, 0) != nullptr) {
-    Tcl_DeleteCommand(interp_, "exit");
-    const std::string restore
-        = std::string("rename ") + kRenamedExitCmd + " exit";
-    Tcl_Eval(interp_, restore.c_str());
+  // to call multiple times).  An `exit` evaluated on an io thread
+  // (tclExitHandler) wakes waitForStop() while that thread is still
+  // inside Tcl_Eval; touching the interpreter before it returns corrupts
+  // Tcl's stack ("TclStackFree: incorrect freePtr", then signal 11).
+  // TclEvaluator::eval holds the mutex for the whole evaluation.
+  {
+    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(tcl_eval_->mutex);
+    if (Tcl_FindCommand(interp_, kRenamedExitCmd, nullptr, 0) != nullptr) {
+      Tcl_DeleteCommand(interp_, "exit");
+      const std::string restore
+          = std::string("rename ") + kRenamedExitCmd + " exit";
+      Tcl_Eval(interp_, restore.c_str());
+    }
   }
 
   tcl_eval_->script_gate.setOnChange({});
